      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Emmanuel Episcopal Church, a Carpenter Gothic landmark, was moved to Jenkins Bridge in 1887 and now sits at the community's center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jenkins_Bridge%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The church preserves a 1749 silver chalice from London that once belonged to the original Assawoman Church of England.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jenkins_Bridge%2C_Virginia",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Holdens Creek, a tidal inlet, flows west into Pocomoke Sound and connects to Chesapeake Bay, shaping the local estuarine ecosystem.",
